Comment:
 This package bundles third-party components, which Debian Policy and the
 Fedora packaging guidelines ask a package to declare rather than hide. They
 are listed here in full.
 .
 /usr/bin/fermix-desktop is a Rust executable. It links the host's GTK and
 libadwaita dynamically, which is why the package declares a versioned relation
 on both rather than carrying a copy of either. Statically linked into it are
 this project's own code and the Rust crates it depends on, each under its own
 licence, all of them MIT or Apache License 2.0; Cargo.lock names every one.
 .
 The executable also carries one compiled resource bundle, whose contents are:
 .
   * The application icon and its symbolic pair, and the Fermix mascot and
     wordmark. Tezra's own artwork, MIT License with this package.
   * Vendor marks for the providers, channels, plugins, sign-in clients and
     meeting platforms the application draws rows for. Each file is the
     vendor's own, redistributed unmodified under that vendor's brand terms;
     App/Fermix/resources/VendorMarks/PROVENANCE.json records the source, the
     retrieval date, the usage terms and the permitted treatment of every one
     of them, and no mark is recoloured, redrawn or invented.
   * One stylesheet, which sets no colour and no font.
 .
 The application contains no engine. The fermix package carries that, and this
 package declares an exact-version dependency on it, so the two always move
 together.
